# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys -- Avast Omni, baked into the image.
#
# This file is PER-SLOT (it lives in the rootfs, not on /data), and that is
# deliberate. sshd is configured with
#     AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys /data/ssh/authorized_keys
# so keys can come from either place:
#
#   * THIS file guarantees access to any slot that boots, even if /data is
#     missing, unmounted or empty -- /data is nofail in fstab precisely so a bad
#     p3 cannot stop the box booting, which would otherwise take SSH with it.
#   * /data/ssh/authorized_keys is for keys added per-device after deployment;
#     those survive an A/B flip but depend on p3 mounting.
#
# Password authentication is OFF (sshd_config.d/10-omni.conf) and the root
# password is locked to '*' at build time, so THIS FILE IS THE ONLY WAY IN OVER
# THE NETWORK. An image that ships with no key here and nothing on /data is
# reachable only over the serial console. check-image-invariants.sh fails the
# build if that happens.
#
# Public keys only. Never put a private key in this repo.

